---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: "Privacy Policy",
  description: "How EduGlossary handles data, cookies, analytics, and advertising.",
};

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: "Home", href: "/" },
  { label: "Privacy Policy", href: "/privacy-policy/" },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How EduGlossary handles data, cookies, analytics, and advertising."
  schema={schema}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: October 13, 2026</em></p>

    <p>
      This policy explains what information EduGlossary (eduglossary.my.id) collects when you
      visit the site, why, and the choices you have. The site is operated by the
      <a href="/authors/eduglossary-team/">EduGlossary Team</a>. You can reach us at
      <a href="mailto:admin@eduglossary.my.id">admin@eduglossary.my.id</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>
      EduGlossary has no user accounts, no comments, and no forms that collect personal details.
      We do not ask you for your name or email address to read the site. If you email us, we
      receive the address and the content of your message and use them only to reply.
    </p>
    <p>
      As with most websites, your browser sends technical information when it loads a page, such
      as your IP address, browser type, device type, referring page, and the pages you view. Some
      of this is processed by the third-party services listed below.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      CookieYes displays a consent banner that lets you choose whether to allow non-essential
      cookies and similar technologies. Your choice is stored by the consent-management service.
      Strictly necessary technologies may operate without consent where permitted by applicable
      law. Analytics and advertising technologies should remain blocked unless the relevant
      consent has been granted. You can reopen the consent choices using the Cookie Settings
      control in the site footer.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google tag and Google Analytics 4 (GA4)</strong> measure how visitors use the
        site (pages viewed, approximate location, device and browser). The site loads the Google tag
        directly after consent; it does not use a Google Tag Manager container. Cookies such as
        <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code> are used after you consent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> provides usage insights such as heatmaps and session
        replays to help us improve the site. Cookies such as <code>_clck</code> and
        <code>_clsk</code> are used after you consent. See the
        <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="noopener">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google AdSense</strong> may show advertising on the site. Google and its partners
        may use cookies and similar technologies to serve and measure ads and, with your consent,
        to personalize them. Without consent, ads may be limited or non-personalized. Learn more at
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>
        and manage ad settings at
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">adssettings.google.com</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>CookieYes</strong> provides the consent banner and stores your consent choice. See
        the <a href="https://www.cookieyes.com/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">CookieYes Privacy Policy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare</strong> delivers and protects the site (content delivery, security,
        and bot protection) and may set a security cookie such as <code>cf_clearance</code>. See the
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <p>
      We use this information to operate and secure the site, understand which content is useful,
      improve the site, and support advertising that helps cover its costs. We do not sell your
      personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Reject non-essential cookies in the consent banner, or select <strong>Cookie Settings</strong>
        in the site footer to reopen the consent choices and change or withdraw your selection.
      </li>
      <li>Delete or block cookies in your browser settings. Some features may stop working.</li>
      <li>
        Opt out of personalized advertising through
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ad Settings</a>
        or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights over your personal data, such as access,
        correction, or deletion. To make a request, email us at
        <a href="mailto:admin@eduglossary.my.id">admin@eduglossary.my.id</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      We do not keep personal data ourselves beyond emails you send us. Data processed by the
      third-party services above is kept according to each service's own policy and settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      EduGlossary is an educational website for a general audience. Visitors do not need to
      provide personal information to read the site, and we do not knowingly collect personal
      information directly from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal
      information to us, please contact
      <a href="mailto:admin@eduglossary.my.id">admin@eduglossary.my.id</a> so we can review the
      matter and take appropriate steps.
    </p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      The site may link to other websites. We are not responsible for their privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The date at the top indicates when it
      was last updated. We encourage you to review this page periodically to stay informed about
      our privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy? See our <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page or email
      <a href="mailto:admin@eduglossary.my.id">admin@eduglossary.my.id</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
